OmniAgent does not include Cordis, the DSH plugin loader, profile/bundle system,
patch system, or DSH runtime packages. The following core modules were
implemented independently, using DSH behavior and public source as design
references rather than copying source files:

- packages/core/src/session/: JSONL event-log and recovery behavior, informed by
  DSH session and JSONL persistence contracts.
- packages/core/src/context/: token pressure estimation and balanced tool-pair
  retention, informed by DSH token-meter and compaction behavior.
- packages/core/src/sandbox/: fail-closed platform sandbox selection, informed
  by DSH sandbox policy and local runner behavior.
- packages/core/src/skills/: progressive skill discovery/loading, informed by
  DSH filesystem skill behavior.
- packages/web/: local UI/API boundary and React Web client. The Web frontend
  reuses DSH's presentational layer directly instead of recreating it; it does
  not include the DSH Web runtime or Cordis client integration.

Copied DSH source is kept under packages/web/ui/vendor/ (ui-theme styles,
Cordis-free ui-primitives React atoms, icon artwork, and shared UI utilities)
and packages/web/ui/src/styles/dsh/ (the CSS modules for app frame, sidebar,
chat view, message items, reasoning rows, turn process/tail/trigger, tool rows,
tool details/tree, assistant markdown, input bar, hero shell, approval panel,
model/permission selectors, permission rows, plan mode, plan preview, todo
panel, and chat groups). These files are copied from DSH's ui-sidebar,
ui-workspace, ui-conversation, ui-settings-general, ui-approval, ui-trajectory,
session-log-export, and client/ui-primitives packages, with only import-path and
runtime-boundary adjustments. Adapted source is distributed under the DSH MIT
license below.

